-- title:
--   Freeness of the Σ-corner of H¹(Γ₀(M),𝒪)
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field, let $p$ be an odd prime with $p \in \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional residual Galois representation over the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$ which is absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to an algebraic closure). Let $S$ be a finite set of primes with $p \in S$, and $M$ a nonzero level all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$, with $p^2 \nmid M$. Let $S_{\min} \subseteq S$ contain $p$ and satisfy, for primes $q \neq p$, $q \in S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$ (some inertia element at some place over $q$ acts nontrivially); every $q \in S_{\min}$ with $q \neq p$ divides $M$; a prime $q \neq p$ outside $S_{\min}$ dividing $M$ divides it at least to the second power; no prime $q \neq p$ with $q^2 \mid M$ has $q^3 \mid M$; at each $q \in S_{\min}$, $q \neq p$, inertia acts with characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$; and if $p \mid M$ then $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$ (a decomposition-stable free rank-one line on which inertia acts trivially modulo that line). Let $r$ be a prime with $r \notin S$ and $r \nmid M$. Assume weight-two cusp forms of level $\Gamma_0(M)$ are spanned over $\mathbb{C}$ by the forms with integral $q$-expansion coefficients, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra of level $M$, weight $2$ away from $S$ to the residue field such that for every prime $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\ell$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Let $\mathbb{T}_0$ be a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, finite over $\mathcal{O}$, acting on $H^1 = \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_0(M)^{\mathrm{ab}}, \mathcal{O})$ compatibly with $\mathcal{O}$, every element of $\mathbb{T}_0$ acting through the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra generated by the operator family indexed by the generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S \cup \{r\}$), $U_q$ ($q \mid M$) and $\langle d \rangle$ ($d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$). Let $\mathrm{Sp}_0$ be an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb{T}_0$ (complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_i$ exhausting all maximal ideals, with $e_i \in \mathfrak{m}_j$ iff $i \neq j$) and $i_0$ an index whose corner submodule $e_{i_0} \cdot H^1$ is finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$. Assume given lifts $t_0(g) \in \mathbb{T}_0$ acting as the operator attached to each generator $g$, and scalars $c_0(g) \in \mathcal{O}$ with $t_0(g) - c_0(g) \in \mathfrak{m}_{i_0}$; cofullness, namely any $v \in H^1$ for which each $g$ and each $k$ admit $n$ with $(t_0(g) - c_0(g))^n \cdot v \in \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}^k \cdot H^1$ lies in $e_{i_0} \cdot H^1$; that $e_{i_0} \cdot H^1 \neq 0$; and that the corner ring at $i_0$ acts faithfully on $e_{i_0} \cdot H^1$. Finally assume the residues of the scalars have $\Sigma$-shape: the residue of $c_0(T_\ell)$ equals $\theta(T_\ell)$ for primes $\ell \nmid M$ outside $S \cup \{r\}$, $c_0(U_q) \in \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ for primes $q \mid M$ with $q \neq p$ and $q^2 \mid M$, $c_0(U_p)$ is a unit when $p \mid M$, and $c_0(\langle d \rangle) - 1 \in \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ for all $d$. Then $e_{i_0} \cdot H^1$ is free as a module over the corner ring of $\mathbb{T}_0$ at $i_0$.
--
--   This is the multiplicity-one statement at level $M$ and trivial character group: the $\Sigma$-corner of the weight-two cohomology $H^1(\Gamma_0(M), \mathcal{O})$ cut out by an absolutely irreducible residual eigensystem is free over the corresponding corner of the Hecke ring, in the shape of Wiles' Theorem 2.1. It is the level-$M$ landing point for the freeness results at auxiliary level $Mr$, and is invoked by [`CohCarrier.free_ordinary_sigmaCorner_level_mul`](thm.html#CohCarrier.free_ordinary_sigmaCorner_level_mul).
